{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00565",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.81,
      "end_seconds": 8.46,
      "duration_seconds": 7.65,
      "text": "It's the shoulder pain again, doctor. Eased off for a couple of weeks, then crept back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.89,
      "end_seconds": 20.38,
      "duration_seconds": 10.49,
      "text": "Come in, sit down. So it settled for a while after last time, and now it's returned. Tell me what it's doing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.33,
      "end_seconds": 28.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.96,
      "text": "Aching, deep inside. Worse at night, lying on it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.84,
      "end_seconds": 38.22,
      "duration_seconds": 7.38,
      "text": "That sounds miserable, your sleep must be suffering. Where exactly would you point to?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.72,
      "end_seconds": 47.67,
      "duration_seconds": 7.95,
      "text": "Here. Top of the arm, at the front, a bit round the back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.79,
      "end_seconds": 59.05,
      "duration_seconds": 9.26,
      "text": "Thank you. Is it the pain that bothers you most, or more the way the shoulder moves?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.04,
      "end_seconds": 67.84,
      "duration_seconds": 6.8,
      "text": "Stiffness too. In the mornings. Takes an hour to loosen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.02,
      "end_seconds": 78.68,
      "duration_seconds": 8.66,
      "text": "An hour, I see. And how would you rate the stiffness, mild, moderate, or worse than that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.07,
      "end_seconds": 84.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Moderate. Getting dressed is the worst bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.34,
      "end_seconds": 96.79,
      "duration_seconds": 10.45,
      "text": "Mm. Getting dressed is a good test, because it needs reaching behind and overhead, which a stiff shoulder hates."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.66,
      "end_seconds": 102.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Yes. Pulling a jumper over my head."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.46,
      "end_seconds": 111.75,
      "duration_seconds": 6.29,
      "text": "Right. And what are you taking for it at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.66,
      "end_seconds": 115.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Paracetamol. When it's bad."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.11,
      "end_seconds": 123.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "Is that helping, or just taking the edge off?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.52,
      "end_seconds": 128.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Edge off. That's all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.27,
      "end_seconds": 139.12,
      "duration_seconds": 9.85,
      "text": "Fair enough. Any allergies to medicines I should know about, before we talk about anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.21,
      "end_seconds": 142.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "None."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.61,
      "end_seconds": 152.57,
      "duration_seconds": 7.96,
      "text": "Good. And the rest of you, any trouble with your breathing at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.79,
      "end_seconds": 155.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.18,
      "end_seconds": 168.68,
      "duration_seconds": 11.5,
      "text": "Lovely. Now let me look at the shoulder. Lift your arm out to the side for me, slowly, and stop when it hurts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.87,
      "end_seconds": 175.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "Okay. Ow. That's as far as it goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.54,
      "end_seconds": 203.96,
      "duration_seconds": 11.42,
      "text": "Your shoulder movement is limited, it stops about halfway and the joint feels tight when I move it for you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.61,
      "end_seconds": 207.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Is that bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.64,
      "end_seconds": 224.08,
      "duration_seconds": 13.44,
      "text": "Not bad as such, but I can't rule out a frozen shoulder at this stage. Picture the joint capsule like a jumper that shrank in the wash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.03,
      "end_seconds": 231.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "Right. How long does that take to go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.13,
      "end_seconds": 242.27,
      "duration_seconds": 10.14,
      "text": "It can take months, I'm afraid, but most people get back to normal movement in the end."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.57,
      "end_seconds": 245.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Months. Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.81,
      "end_seconds": 260.44,
      "duration_seconds": 13.63,
      "text": "Meanwhile, keep it moving. Gentle pendulum swings with the arm hanging down, a few minutes each day, and sleep on your other side hugging a pillow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.11,
      "end_seconds": 264.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "I can do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.11,
      "end_seconds": 274.71,
      "duration_seconds": 7.6,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in six weeks, to check how much it has loosened."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.32,
      "end_seconds": 279.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Alright. Six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.75,
      "end_seconds": 290.54,
      "duration_seconds": 8.79,
      "text": "The receptionist will book that for you on your way out. Have you got any questions for me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.93,
      "end_seconds": 294.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "No. Thanks, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.82,
      "end_seconds": 302.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Take care, and be kind to that shoulder."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.74,
      "end_seconds": 305.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Will do. Bye."
    }
  ]
}
